<div class="shell">
  <section class="card lede">
    <h2>Four questions to ask any AI tool before you put anything into it.</h2>
    <p><b>Who made it</b> and who owns it now. <b>Why it was made</b> — and how it makes money, which is usually the more revealing question. <b>Where what you type goes</b> — which model provider receives it, in which country. <b>Whether it trains on you</b>, and whether you can take that back.</p>
    <p>Twenty-eight reference cards are below, each answering all four from the vendor's own published policy. The striking result: <b>ten of the twenty-eight do not say, anywhere findable, whether your input trains a model</b> — and most of those are the specialist systematic review platforms, where the input is unpublished research data.</p>
  </section>

