ore, Australia, India, or UAE**; API customers can select processing regions. [business data](https://openai.com/business-data/)","training":"**Split by tier.** Business tiers: **no by default** — \"We do not use data from ChatGPT Enterprise, ChatGPT Business, ChatGPT Edu, ChatGPT for Healthcare, ChatGPT for Teachers, or our API platform—including inputs or outputs—for training or improving our models by default\"; opt-in available. **Free/Plus/Pro consumer accounts are trained on by default with a user-facing opt-out** in data controls. [business data](https://openai.com/business-data/)","retention":"Configurable retention for qualifying organisations, including **zero data retention on the API**. Consumer deletion available in-app (~30 days to purge). ⚠️ **Documented complication:** a 2025 preservation order in *NYT v. OpenAI* required retention of output-log data including deleted consumer chats; reporting indicates the order was lifted around 23 Oct 2025, with exceptions for already-preserved data. Verify current status before relying on deletion. [OpenAI response](https://openai.com/index/response-to-nyt-data-demands/) · [Engadget, Oct 2025](https://www.engadget.com/ai/openai-no-longer-has-to-preserve-all-of-its-chatgpt-data-with-some-exceptions-192422093.html)","compliance":"**SOC 2 Type 2; ISO/IEC 27001, 27017, 27018, 27701**; GDPR/CCPA support with DPA; **BAA available for HIPAA** (Healthcare products). **Public trust portal at trust.openai.com.** **FERPA:** ChatGPT for Teachers is \"built to protect student data and help schools meet FERPA requirements\". [business data](https://openai.com/business-data/) · [trust portal](https://trust.openai.com/) · [ChatGPT for Teachers](https://openai.com/index/chatgpt-for-teachers/)","open":0,"ferpa":2,"incident":"A preservation order in NYT v. OpenAI required retention of output logs including consumer chats users had deleted, overriding the 30-day deletion practice. Reporting indicates the order was lifted around 23 October 2025. A vendor's deletion promise can be suspended by litigation it is not party to.","lOwn":1,"lDest":2,"lTrain":2,"tscore":5},"gemini":{"name":"Google Gemini","entity":"Google LLC / Alphabet","url":"https://gemini.google.com","who":"Google LLC, subsidiary of **Alphabet Inc.** (NASDAQ: GOOGL); Gemini models from Google DeepMind. Publicly listed; no external funding relevant.","why":"General-purpose assistant across consumer and Workspace products. Business model: advertising-funded core business, consumer subscription (Google AI Plus/Pro/Ultra), Workspace seat licensing, and Vertex AI/API usage billing.","where":"Google-operated infrastructure. For consumer Gemini Apps: **\"A subset of chats are reviewed by human reviewers\"**, and \"chats are disconnected from your account before being sent to service providers.\" For Workspace/Gemini Enterprise: customers \"can control where their data is stored and processed (**EU or US**)\" and can restrict support-personnel access by region. [Gemini Apps privacy hub](https://support.google.com/gemini/answer/13594961?hl=en) · [Workspace AI privacy](https://workspace.google.com/security/ai-privacy/)","training":"**Split sharply by account type.** **Consumer: yes by default.** With \"Keep Activity\" on (the default), conversations feed model development — \"These uses extend to the generative AI models and other machine-learning technologies powering our services.\" Turning Keep Activity off or using temporary chats stops this (except where you submit feedback). **Workspace/Education: no** — \"Google does **not** use customers' Workspace data to train or improve the underlying generative AI and large language models… outside of Workspace without permission\", and data \"is not reviewed by humans.\" [Gemini privacy hub](https://support.google.com/gemini/answer/13594961?hl=en) · [Workspace AI privacy](https://workspace.google.com/security/ai-privacy/)","retention":"Consumer with Keep Activity on: auto-delete at **18 months**