ctive — the help centre states plainly that opt-outs apply only to data collected after the opt-out date. Combined with training on by default for Free/Pro/Max, this is the weakest consumer position among the general assistants.","lOwn":1,"lDest":2,"lTrain":2,"tscore":5},"copilot":{"name":"Microsoft Copilot","entity":"Microsoft Corporation","url":"https://copilot.microsoft.com","who":"Microsoft Corporation (NASDAQ: MSFT), founded 1975, HQ Redmond WA. Publicly listed. Copilot is built on OpenAI models under Microsoft's OpenAI partnership, plus Microsoft's own and (newly) Anthropic models as subprocessors.","why":"AI assistant embedded across Microsoft 365, Windows and Bing. Business model: per-seat licence add-on to Microsoft 365 commercial/education, free consumer Copilot, and Azure AI Foundry consumption billing.","where":"Microsoft-operated Azure infrastructure. \"For European Union (EU) users, we have additional safeguards to comply with the **EU Data Boundary**. EU traffic stays within the EU Data Boundary while worldwide traffic can be sent to the EU and other countries or regions for LLM processing.\" ⚠️ **\"Models provided by Anthropic as a subprocessor are currently excluded from the EU Data Boundary.\"** Copilot was added to Microsoft's data-residency commitments in Product Terms on 1 Mar 2024. [Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/copilot/microsoft-365/microsoft-365-copilot-privacy)","training":"**No, for commercial/365 Copilot.** \"Prompts, responses, and data accessed through Microsoft Graph **aren't used to train foundation LLMs**, including those used by Microsoft Copilot\"; \"Your personal data collected from the use of connected experiences in Microsoft 365 isn't used to train large language models.\" **Consumer Copilot (free, personal Microsoft account) has different terms — UNVERIFIED here; do not assume parity.** [Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/copilot/microsoft-365/microsoft-365-copilot-privacy)","retention":"Prompts and responses are stored, including citations. Admins set retention via **Microsoft Purview**; users can delete Copilot activity history in the My Account portal. **No default period stated — partly UNVERIFIED.**","compliance":"\"**GDPR, ISO 27001, HIPAA, and the ISO 42001** standard for AI management systems\"; commitment to EU AI Act compliance; Purview Information Protection sensitivity labels honoured. **FERPA is not mentioned** in the privacy documentation — Microsoft offers FERPA-aligned terms for Education SKUs generally, but that is **UNVERIFIED at the Copilot level**. Public trust centre: microsoft.com/trust-center. [Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/copilot/microsoft-365/microsoft-365-copilot-privacy)","open":0,"ferpa":1,"incident":"Microsoft documents that models provided by Anthropic as a subprocessor are currently excluded from the EU Data Boundary, so some Copilot traffic leaves the boundary despite the general commitment.","lOwn":2,"lDest":2,"lTrain":1,"tscore":5},"notebooklm":{"name":"NotebookLM","entity":"Google","url":"https://notebooklm.google.com","who":"Google LLC / Alphabet Inc. Originated as \"Project Tailwind\" from Google Labs (2023). No separate entity or funding.","why":"Source-grounded research and notetaking assistant: answers restricted to documents the user uploads. Business model: free consumer tier; **NotebookLM Plus** bundled into Google Workspace/AI subscriptions.","where":"Google infrastructure. **Workspace editions:** \"Your data remains your data and any files uploaded, queries and responses are **not shared outside your organization's trust boundary**.\" Data residency controls (EU or US) available on Workspace/Gemini Enterprise. **Consumer NotebookLM residency: UNVERIFIED.** [Workspace core service announcement](https://workspaceupdates.googleblog.com/2025/02/notebooklm-and-notebooklm-plus-now-workspace-core-service.html) · [Workspace AI privacy](https://workspace.google.com/security/ai-privacy/)","training":"**Split by account type.** **Workspace: no** — \"Your uploads, queries and the model's responses are **not used to train models** and are **not reviewed by human reviewers** or otherwise used for product improvement **without permission**.\" Covered editions: NotebookLM in Business Starter, Frontline Starter/Standard, Essentials tiers, Nonprofits; NotebookLM Plus in Business Standard/Plus, Enterprise Standard/Plus. **Consumer (personal Google account): UNVERIFIED — the consumer NotebookLM terms are not covered by the Workspace statement and should be checked separately before uploading unpublished data.** [core service announcement](https://workspaceupdates.googleblog.com/2025/02/notebooklm-and-notebooklm-plus-now-workspace-core-service.html)","retention":"Notebooks and sources deletable by the user. **Retention periods: UNVERIFIED.**","compliance":"As a **Workspace core service**, it is \"covered under your Google Workspace terms of service\" with \"enterprise-grade data protections\" — meaning it inherits Workspace's DPA, ISO 42001, BSI C5, FedRAMP High, HIPAA support and, for Education editions, Workspace's FERPA-aligned terms. Consumer tier: no such coverage. [core service announcement](https://workspaceupdates.googleblog.com/2025/02/notebooklm-and-notebooklm-plus-now-workspace-core-service.html) · [Workspace AI privacy](https://workspace.google.com/security/ai-privacy/)","open":0,"ferpa":1,"incident":"","lOwn":2,"lDest":2,"lTrain":1,"tscore":5}};
